pip is fully functional now.

**What was wrong:** The `pip` Python package files (the actual `pip/` module directory) were missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`. Only the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) remained, which is why Python reported pip as "already installed" but couldn't import it.

**What I did:** Removed the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which extracted the bundled `pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl` into site-packages. pip is now working and can install packages.

